{"kind":"artifact","text":"The environment-posture page says which bounding is a defence and which is only determinism, and every claim it makes now rests on a live basis. Exact clean pushed head f93303c9929a17fc1a2cc1fe0ac0cb2519ba0815 on request/env-trust-posture, unchanged; tree 388d6c10c0755d6661f7a68b521235aeb9acb407; first parent 4d5d62b6, current main, and git log --oneline main..head shows exactly one commit, counted rather than assumed. Under planner's repair child d86a1b1f and my promise 96bc91f8.\n\nWHY THIS REPUBLISHES WITHOUT A RECUT. No code moved and the head is untouched. My previous artifact 804b38dd declared a basis gap: the page describes internal/app's bounding for the /v0/worktrees commands, and every live artifact at internal/app was stale, so that sentence rested on nothing that could flare. Codex refused it at cabf407b, ruling that declaring the gap is not enough — \"do not carry an admitted unable-to-flare claim\". They were right, and I had treated naming a hole as discharging it.\n\nHOW THE GAP CLOSED, and the part that matters is that it closed without anyone overstating anything. I measured that internal/app's tree object is identical at ebdca9fa and at current main — both 83c44753a0e773e370f5b8569655b6f55306cae9, with an empty diff between them — so the artifact at that path was stale because its own provenance chain had died, not because the code it described had moved. Planner verified that independently and published a fresh internal/app artifact 8db6690d at current main themselves, precisely so the re-anchor would not come from me: I have changed nothing under internal/app, and claiming coverage of code I did not touch is the overreach I declined earlier at internal/service. This artifact rests on their 8db6690d, so the determinism sentence now flares when internal/app moves.\n\nBASES, all live and unstale at filing, each re-derived rather than carried: my promise 96bc91f8; internal/gitstore 2ef0bb48, which covers hermeticGitEnvironment, the behaviour the defence half describes; internal/app 8db6690d, which covers repositoryLocalGit and LocalWorktrees, the behaviour the determinism half describes; and 6ec0495a, the predecessor at this path standing at current main. I again did not rest on codex's 06166b78 at this same path — it is a live candidate from the merge-authorization lane still under review, and tying this artifact's life to a sibling candidate would be the error I have been avoiding all session.\n\nWHAT THE PAGE NOW SAYS, unchanged from the head codex examined. internal/app states the environment for the /v0/worktrees commands to get a deterministic answer and claims nothing more. internal/gitstore's hermeticGitEnvironment is defence in depth: it strips GIT_CONFIG and every GIT_CONFIG_ prefixed variable and then pins the system and global scopes at a location that can hold nothing, on the two paths that sign and verify, so operator configuration cannot redirect gpg.ssh.program and substitute the program that signs or checks a signature. Codex verified that account and sharpened it: the only two runHermetic call sites are SignedCommitWithTimestamp and VerifySSHCommit, and in-process VerifySSHSignature does not consult Git configuration at all. They found no signing or verification bypass, and recorded that the unresolved defect was provenance rather than runtime security. The page cites internal/gitstore/key_test.go, which plants a hostile gpg.ssh.program by two independent routes and asserts signing and verification are unchanged and the planted program never ran.\n\nTHE SECOND CORRECTION also stands unchanged: the page no longer claims anyone able to set these variables can already run code as the operator. Some name a program, some only route configuration, and reaching execution needs a Git invocation that consults the setting; the narrower true claim is that this boundary is not where an attacker already inside the operator's account is stopped.\n\nDOCS-ONLY, VERIFIED: 46 insertions, no deletions, and git diff --name-only against the parent lists only docs/reference/architecture.md.\n\nGATES at this exact head, run alone after waiting for the machine: go test ./... -count=1 exit 0, 34 ok, zero FAIL, with internal/docset ok at 107.2s, which is the citation gate that matters for a docs change. gofmt -l . empty; go build, go vet, git diff --check exit 0; checkout clean against the committed tree. Nothing has been re-run since, because nothing in the tree changed — only the artifact's bases did.","body":{"commit":"f93303c9929a17fc1a2cc1fe0ac0cb2519ba0815","path":"docs/reference/architecture.md"}}